# =============================================================================
# CardioScope dashboard -- .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# NOTE ON THE MODEL FILE: models/artifacts/dv_severity_model_improved.joblib
# is ~8MB, well under GitHub's 100MB per-file limit -- it is intentionally
# NOT excluded here and NOT using Git LFS. It's part of what makes the app
# actually work when someone clones this repo, so it's meant to be tracked
# normally. If a future, much larger model is swapped in (e.g. >50-100MB),
# switch to Git LFS at that point (`git lfs track "*.joblib"`).
# =============================================================================

# ---- Python environments ----
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# ---- OS / editor cruft ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ---- Streamlit ----
.streamlit/secrets.toml   # never commit secrets/API keys if any are added later

# ---- Local runtime output (not source, regenerated at runtime) ----
reports/*.pdf
reports/*.html
!reports/README.md        # keep the explanatory README, exclude only generated output

# ---- Real patient / test ECG data -- NEVER commit real recordings ----
# The only ECG data that should ever be tracked in this repo is the
# synthetically-generated demo waveform, which is created in-code
# (utils/ecg_loader.load_sample_ecg()) and is never written to disk as a
# file in the first place. Any real .hea/.dat/.mat/.csv ECG files -- test
# downloads, real dataset samples, anything from a real patient -- must
# never be committed. These patterns catch them if anyone drops one into
# the project folder to test locally:
*.hea
*.dat
*.mat
sample_uploads/
test_data/
local_test_records/
# If you genuinely need a real WFDB pair tracked for automated testing,
# add an explicit exception here for that specific file only (matching
# the pattern already used for the model artefact above) -- never a
# blanket allow.

# ---- Local env/config ----
.env
.env.local
*.local
